shell_coupling.py:\n\n```python\nPLASTIC_DC_TARGET = -11.0 / 60.0\nPLASTIC_DC_STEPS = 11\nPLASTIC_PREFIX_TARGET = -0.10\nPLASTIC_PREFIX_STEPS = 6\nPLASTIC_RESUME_STEPS = 5\nPLASTIC_MAX_ITERATIONS = 40\nCASES = (\"preyield\", \"plastic\")\nSTAGES = (\"full\", \"prefix\")\n```\n\n_AcceptedHistory: add control_value tracking.\n\n```python\ndef run_plastic(\n    coupling=DEFAULT_COUPLING, *, stage=\"full\", restart=None, checkpoint_out=None,\n    cancellation_token=None, progress_callback=None,\n) -> dict:\n    if stage not in STAGES: raise ValueError(...)\n    if restart is not None and stage != \"full\": raise ValueError(\"--restart resumes toward the full target; stage must be 'full'\")\n    case = build_model(coupling)\n    history = _AcceptedHistory(progress_callback)\n    if restart is not None:\n        with open(restart, \"rb\") as s: checkpoint_bytes = s.read()\n        target = PLASTIC_DC_TARGET\n        num_steps = PLASTIC_RESUME_STEPS\n    elif stage == \"prefix\":\n        target = PLASTIC_PREFIX_TARGET; num_steps = PLASTIC_PREFIX_STEPS\n    else:\n        target = PLASTIC_DC_TARGET; num_steps = PLASTIC_DC_STEPS\n    control = DisplacementControl(node_id=case.probe_node_id, dof=\"uz\", target_displacement=target)\n    try:\n        result = solve_static_nonlinear(\n            case.model, case.load, control=\"displacement\", displacement_control=control,\n            kinematics=\"corotational\", num_steps=num_steps,\n            max_iterations=PLASTIC_MAX_ITERATIONS, tolerance=TOLERANCE,\n            record_increment_snapshots=True,\n            restart_checkpoint=checkpoint_bytes if restart is not None else None,\n            emit_restart_checkpoint=checkpoint_out is not None,\n            cancellation_token=cancellation_token,\n            progress_callback=history,\n        )\n    except SolveCancelled as cancelled:\n        achieved = history.last_accepted_control_value\n        return {...status cancelled...}\n    ...\n```\n\nWait — restart refusal ValueError propagates from solve_static_nonlinear. Catch it in run_plastic? If I catch ValueError there, the payload gets status \"restart_refused\". But ValueError could also arise from genuine misuse. I'll catch it and mark status \"restart_refused\" with stop_reason — truthful either way. Hmm, but for the CLI the distinction matters little; exit 1.\n\nActually — cleaner: let run_plastic raise, and CLI catches? No — run() catches SolveCancelled and returns payload; symmetric design: run_plastic catches SolveCancelled → \"cancelled\" payload; catches ValueError → \"restart_refused\" payload. But a ValueError from a bad flag combination inside build (e.g. unknown coupling) should still raise... build_model raises ValueError for unknown coupling before the try. OK.\n\nPayload completed criteria:\n```python\nachieved_uz = _probe_uz(case, result.displacements)\ncontrol_error = abs(achieved_uz - target)\ncompleted = (result.status == \"completed\" and control_error <= COMPLETION_LOAD_FACTOR_TOL\n             and postcheck passed)\n```\nCOMPLETION_LOAD_FACTOR_TOL = 1e-8 — same value used for target error. Name it TARGET_ERROR_TOL = 1e-8? Reuse COMPLETION_LOAD_FACTOR_TOL (1e-8). I'll add `COMPLETION_TARGET_TOL = 1.0e-8` alias... simpler: use the existing constant.\n\nmax_equivalent_plastic_strain: from result.steps[-1].max_equivalent_plastic_strain if steps else 0.0? For cancelled: history could track it from events. Events carry max_equivalent_plastic_strain. Track last accepted in history.\n\nCheckpoint write:\n```python\ncheckpoint_written = None\nif completed and checkpoint_out is not None:\n    raw = result.restart_checkpoint_bytes()\n    with open(checkpoint_out, \"wb\") as stream: stream.write(raw)\n    checkpoint_written = str(checkpoint_out)\n```\n\nFor cancelled payload: include requested_displacement, achieved_displacement (last accepted control value or None), control_error (None if no achieved), accepted_increments, load_factor (last accepted or None), max_equivalent_plastic_strain (last accepted or None), completed False, checkpoint None.\n\nmain() CLI:\n\n```python\nparser.add_argument(\"--case\", choices=CASES, default=\"preyield\", ...)\nparser.add_argument(\"--stage\", choices=STAGES, default=\"full\", ...)\nparser.add_argument(\"--restart\", default=None, ...)\nparser.add_argument(\"--checkpoint-out\", default=None, ...)\nargs = parser.parse_args(argv)\nif args.checkpoint_out is not None and args.case != \"plastic\":\n    parser.error(\"--checkpoint-out requires --case plastic ...\")\nif args.restart is not None:\n    if args.case != \"plastic\": parser.error(...)\n    if args.stage != \"full\": parser.error(...)\n    if not Path(args.restart).is_file(): parser.error(f\"--restart file not found: {args.restart}\")\nif args.case == \"preyield\":\n    payload = run(args.coupling)\nelse:\n    payload = run_plastic(args.coupling, stage=args.stage, restart=args.restart, checkpoint_out=args.checkpoint_out)\n```\n\nNote: existing slice1 test `test_cli_stdout_json_exit_status_and_output_file` monkeypatches `run` in main.__globals__ and calls main([\"--output\", path]) then main([\"--coupling\",\"direct\"]) — with default --case preyield, dispatch still goes to run(). Good, unchanged.\n\n`test_cli_rejects_unknown_coupling` expects SystemExit code 2 — unchanged.\n\nNow the docstring update for the module and run_plastic.\n\nOne more check — `DisplacementControl` export from anysolver top-level: slice3 test imports it from anysolver. Good.\n\nPath import: examples currently don't import Path; use os.path or pathlib. I'll use pathlib.\n\nNow write the code.", "summary": []}
